From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:13:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Hand packets to the event loop through one queue per
 connection

Every packet the server thread sent was a task of its own on the event loop, each with a wake-up
of the loop (eventfd writes were 1.1% of a 20-player server on the VPS). Packets, flushes and
closes now go onto a per-connection queue with one drain task posted when it becomes non-empty.
Order and flush points are exactly as before: a write's listeners run on its flush and some
change the pipeline (set-compression adds the compressor).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

